=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ BESZEL @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt beszel agent @VERSION@ for OpenVMS (vms-beszel): reports this system to a beszel hub
1 'NOTICE
=prompt The beszel agent for OpenVMS is distributed under the MIT licence.
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [BESZEL.DOC]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for the beszel agent (vms-beszel)
    Once, as SYSTEM: create or check the agent's account (default BESZEL, with a
    UIC group of its own above MAXSYSGROUP), set the protections, and create
    BESZEL$ROOT:[CONF]AGENT.CONF from its template:
    $ @BESZEL$ROOT:[COM]BESZEL$CONFIGURE
    Put the hub's address, key and token in BESZEL$ROOT:[CONF]AGENT.CONF
    (from the hub's "Add System" dialog), then:
    $ @BESZEL$ROOT:[COM]BESZEL$CONTROL START
    At boot, add to SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM (after TCP/IP):
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:BESZEL$STARTUP.COM
    At shutdown, add to SYS$MANAGER:SYSHUTDWN.COM:
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:BESZEL$SHUTDOWN.COM

PRODUCT REMOVE BESZEL stops the agent and deassigns BESZEL$ROOT; the
configuration, the fingerprint, the logs and the account are kept.
